dbSta: write_spef names pins and internal nodes by their database names

With hierarchy the network's path names keep only an instance name's
last level (dbNetwork::stripParentPrefix): a cell
h1/core\/dispatch/ff0 in module instance h1 was written h1/ff0, which no
instance is, and its pins were read back unconnected (over 1,000 nets of
XiangShan's tile with OPENROAD_HIERARCHICAL=1). *D_NET already used the
database's net name; *CONN, *CAP and *RES now do too.

Test: write_spef_hier_inst_name.

Carried by bazel-orfs; reported upstream as OpenROAD#12049 with this
fix, not merged. Retires on a
//:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries it.
